{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":200,"text":"**NOS System Map / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\n253 components · 350 canonical relationships · 140 visible arrows\nReal component arrows, capped at 140: retain every app/face ↔ service link, service → store link and driver/task → service link; fill remaining places with inter-lane relationships, prioritising flow pairs, gap endpoints, persistence and app/face coverage. Parallel directed pairs collapse into one labelled arrow. Directions and MISSING labels remain canonical. Focused canvases retain EVERY edge incident to their members, with one-hop neighbours as ghost cards. Cyan data · orange control · green persist · purple schedule · yellow UI · red event. Red card borders mark high/critical gaps.\nGreen working · yellow partial · red stub/broken · grey dead code. Verified gap badges included.","color":"5"},
{"id":"system-index","type":"text","x":0,"y":296,"width":800,"height":344,"text":"**Explore a system / all incident edges**\n\n[[canvases/Health and activity.canvas|Health and activity]]\n[[canvases/Sports and workouts.canvas|Sports and workouts]]\n[[canvases/Power and battery.canvas|Power and battery]]\n[[canvases/Services hub.canvas|Services hub]]\n[[canvases/Storage and persistence.canvas|Storage and persistence]]\n[[canvases/Engine and scheduling.canvas|Engine and scheduling]]\n[[canvases/Connectivity and voice.canvas|Connectivity and voice]]\n[[canvases/Shell and faces.canvas|Shell and faces]]\n[[canvases/Utility apps.canvas|Utility apps]]\n[[canvases/Settings and developer.canvas|Settings and developer]]","color":"6"},
{"id":"ext-open-meteo","type":"text","x":9624,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Open-Meteo API**\nPublic forecast HTTP API used by the watch's…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Queried every 1800 s (60 s after a failure) by the weather task.\n\n`UNKNOWN`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]"},
{"id":"ext-phone-gadgetbridge","type":"text","x":10080,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Phone (Gadgetbridge)**\nAndroid phone running Gadgetbridge…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Lines drained by the watch at up to 8 per services tick.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"ext-llm-api","type":"text","x":10536,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**LLM / STT / TTS API**\nOpenRouter-style cloud API used by voice…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Not reachable on the B build.\n\n`STUB`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"ext-host-tools","type":"text","x":10992,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Host tools (flash_watch, sdsync, exports)**\nPython tools: checked flash helper…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Run by the developer on demand.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|1 gap]]\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"ext-host-pc","type":"text","x":11448,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Host PC (serial, OTA, setup browser)**\nPC on USB serial or the watch's Wi-Fi: sends…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Event driven by the user.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"ext-ntp","type":"text","x":11904,"y":900,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**SNTP time server**\nInternet time source. Once Wi-Fi is up the…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Re-synced about hourly while Wi-Fi is connected.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-ft3168-touch","type":"text","x":7116,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**FT3168 touch (0x38)**\nCapacitive touch on shared I2C…\n\nruns: Hardware. Polled by the touch task: 10 ms when ON, 40 ms otherwise.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-sd-card","type":"text","x":7572,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**SD card (1-bit SDMMC)**\nSD on CLK41/CMD39/D0=40 (D3=38 unused).…\n\nruns: Hardware. Mounted by board-fs; every access goes through a mount lease and lock.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-battery-adc","type":"text","x":8028,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Battery ADC (GPIO4, divider 3)**\nMeasures the system rail on GPIO4 (ADC1 ch3,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Sampled once a second by the battery sampler.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"hw-button","type":"text","x":8484,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**BOOT button (GPIO0)**\nSide button on GPIO0. ISR with 25 ms…\n\nruns: ISR on edge. Works in every display state.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-deep-sleep","type":"text","x":8940,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Deep sleep (ext0 GPIO0 wake)**\nLowest power state, entered only by the…\n\nruns: Only on explicit POWER OFF.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-qmi8658-imu","type":"text","x":9396,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**QMI8658 IMU (0x6B)**\n6-axis accelerometer/gyro, INT on GPIO8 (not…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read about 150 times/s by board-sense, with the screen on or off.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|4 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-co5300-panel","type":"text","x":9852,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n466x466 RGB565 AMOLED on QSPI (CS9, CLK10,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Driven by the flush task; DISPOFF/SLPIN in sleep states.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-pcf85063-rtc","type":"text","x":10308,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**PCF85063 RTC (0x51)**\nBattery-backed calendar chip on shared I2C.…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read once at boot; written when board_clock_changed is set.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-radio","type":"text","x":10764,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**ESP32-S3 Wi-Fi and BLE radio**\nShared 2.4 GHz radio. Wi-Fi station/AP and…\n\nruns: Hardware. Powered per saved Wi-Fi/BLE intent.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-strap-hr","type":"text","x":11220,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: MAX30102 HR/SpO2**\nOptional back-header PPG module. Not…\n\nruns: Hardware. FIFO drained every 120 ms while leased; background read every 10 min.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-gps","type":"text","x":11676,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: GPS (UART)**\nOptional GNSS strap on a UART. Probes three…\n\nruns: Hardware. Powered only while a getter or owner keeps it alive (8 s idle).\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|4 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-lte","type":"text","x":12132,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: Quectel EG800AK LTE**\nOptional LTE modem strap (AT commands, SMS).…\n\nruns: Hardware. Modem off 8 s after the last UI caller.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-env","type":"text","x":12588,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: BME280 baro/temp/humidity**\nOptional environment sensor strap: pressure,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Forced-mode read every 2 s once present.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-light","type":"text","x":13044,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: APDS-9960 light/proximity**\nOptional ambient-light and proximity strap.…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read about every 400 ms by the ext task.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-mag","type":"text","x":13500,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: QMC5883L/HMC5883L compass**\nOptional magnetometer strap for the Compass…\n\nruns: Hardware. Sampled only while a consumer asks.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-haptic","type":"text","x":13956,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: coin ERM haptic motor**\nOptional vibration motor strap driven by PWM…\n\nruns: Hardware. Pattern segments timed by the haptic esp_timer.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]"},
{"id":"hw-strap-audio","type":"text","x":14412,"y":1616,"width":400,"height":248,"text":"**Strap: MAX98357A amp + INMP441 mic**\nOptional I2S speaker and microphone strap…\n\nruns: Hardware. I2S pumped in 4 ms blocks while recording or playing.\n\n`UNKNOWN` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]"},
{"id":"drv-board","type":"text","x":5292,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Board device layer (board.c)**\nOwns I2C devices and creates the board-sense…\n\nruns: Library code called from board-sense, board-fs and the UI loop.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-hal-esp32","type":"text","x":5748,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**HAL glue (hal_esp32.c)**\nImplements the core/hal.h contract on ESP-…\n\nruns: Library code called from every task.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-sd","type":"text","x":6204,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**SD mount, lease and lock**\nMounts the card and hands out a mount lease…\n\nruns: board-fs retries a failed mount; leases taken per file operation.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|17 gaps]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"drv-nus","type":"text","x":6660,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**NUS transport and RX line ring**\nNordic UART GATT service. Assembles lines…\n\nruns: Written from nimble_host; read by phone_tick, at most 8 lines per tick.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-display","type":"text","x":7116,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display flush and QSPI panel driver**\nStripe job queue to the flush task,…\n\nruns: Jobs queued by the UI task; executed on the flush task (core 1).\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-display-te","type":"text","x":7572,"y":2332,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display TE wait (no TE on B)**\nTearing-effect synchronisation helper. B…\n\nruns: Never active on B.\n\n`STUB`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"1"},
